@baseUrl = https://localhost:5001

# Oficina API - requests executaveis
#
# Pre-requisitos:
#   1. Execute `docker compose up --build` na raiz do repositorio.
#   2. Confirme GET {{baseUrl}}/health e abra {{baseUrl}}/swagger.
#   3. Execute as requests da secao "Fluxo principal" de cima para baixo.
#   4. Execute a secao "Limpeza opcional" somente ao final e individualmente.
#
# Sintaxe: Visual Studio HTTP files, JetBrains Rider e extensao REST Client do VS Code.
# Os IDs sao obtidos das respostas nomeadas pela expressao
# `nomeDaRequest.response.body.$.propriedade`, entre chaves duplas. Clientes antigos podem nao oferecer
# variaveis de resposta; nesse caso, copie os GUIDs retornados para as URLs.
#
# Os campos document, email, plate e code possuem valores unicos. Se uma execucao
# for interrompida antes da limpeza, conclua a limpeza com os IDs retornados ou
# altere esses valores antes de executar o fluxo novamente.

### Health check (auxiliar; nao faz parte das 38 operacoes do Swagger)

###############################################################################
# Fluxo principal
###############################################################################

GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Notifications - Send simple email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "cliente@example.com"
}

### Issue technical JWT (no user or login)
# @name issueToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/token

### Customers 1/5 - Create customer
# @name createCustomer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{issueToken.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Maria da Silva",
  "email": "maria.oficina@example.com",
  "telephoneNumber": "+5511999990001",
  "document": "529.982.247-25"
}
### Customers 2/5 - List customers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers?search=Maria&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{issueToken.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Customers 3/5 - Get customer by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{issueToken.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Customers 4/5 - Update customer
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{issueToken.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Maria da Silva Atualizada",
  "email": "maria.oficina@example.com",
  "telephoneNumber": "+5511999990002",
  "document": "52998224725"
}

### Vehicles 1/6 - Create vehicle
# @name createVehicle
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles
Authorization: Bearer {{issueToken.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}",
  "plate": "FHT2A31",
  "brand": "Honda",
  "model": "Civic",
  "year": 2022,
  "category": 1
}

### Vehicles 2/6 - Identify customer and register another vehicle
# @name identifyCustomerAndRegisterVehicle
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles/identify-customer-and-register
Authorization: Bearer {{issueToken.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "document": "52998224725",
  "plate": "BRA2E19",
  "brand": "Toyota",
  "model": "Corolla",
  "year": 2023,
  "category": 1
}

### Vehicles 3/6 - List vehicles filtered by customer
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles?page=1&pageSize=20&customerId={{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{issueToken.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Vehicles 4/6 - Get vehicle by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles/{{createVehicle.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{issueToken.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Vehicles 5/6 - Update vehicle
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vehicles/{{createVehicle.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{issueToken.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "plate": "FHT2A31",
  "brand": "Honda",
  "model": "Civic Touring",
  "year": 2022,
  "category": 1
}

